# Act I
dialogue rook
  node root rook "You've got his eyes. Don't look so pleased about it. They never once helped him find the bar."
    > "You knew my father." -> knew
    > "Who are you?" -> who
    > "Sorry. I'm in a hurry." -> bye
  node who rook "Rook. Navigator. Retired, the way a ship's retired when it's on the bottom. I took the Arcadia out of this harbour on her last run."
    set met_rook
    > "You sailed with my father?" -> knew
  node knew rook "I steered for him for eleven years. Best captain on the Straits run, and the worst singer on any of them."
    set met_rook
    -> knew2
  node knew2 rook "I was aboard the Arcadia when she went missing, boy, and she did not sink while I was looking."
    > "Then how are you here?" -> fog
    > "The ledger says she was lost." -> ledger
  node fog rook "Fog came down out of a clear sky. Men rowed out under a yellow flag. 'Quarantine,' ever so polite."
    -> fog2
  node fog2 rook "They took me off first, paid me, put me on a fruit boat. I've been drunk ever since, and it's still the strangest thing I've seen."
    > "Paid you?" -> purse
    > "And the ledger?" -> ledger
  node purse rook "A purse with a little wax cloud on it. Never opened it. Seemed like the one decent thing left to do, and I've been very careful not to do any others."
    note rook_paid "Rook was taken off the Arcadia under a yellow flag, 'for quarantine', and paid off with a purse stamped with a little wax cloud. He never opened it. Quarantine where? Nobody said."
    > "And the ledger?" -> ledger
  node ledger rook "When I got home she was already written in as lost. Three days before she was even late. Ink does what the man holding the pen is paid to."
    -> ledger2
  node ledger2 rook "It's all in the harbour ledger, up in the loft over the chandler's."
    > "The loft's shutter is bolted." if looked:alley.warehouse_stairs -> locked
    > "Who paid?" -> cray
    > "What do I do with it?" -> advice
  node locked rook "Bolted from the lane side, which is the trusting side. A crowbar will talk it round. Crowbars are very persuasive. So I'm told. By crowbars."
    > "Who paid?" -> cray
    > "Thank you. I'll pass that on to the crowbar." -> thanks
  node cray rook "Silas Cray. Factor. He'll be in the lane, being expensive at someone."
    -> cray2
  node cray2 rook "If he offers to buy that compass, ask yourself why a man who owns everything wants the one thing in Vela that points the wrong way."
    > "What do I do with the ledger?" -> advice
    > "Thank you. I'll keep a hand on my pocket." -> thanks
  node advice rook "Read it. Then say it to Bramwick's face, at his own desk. Shame works on men like him. On me it only works on Tuesdays."
    > "Who paid for the entry?" -> cray
    > "Thank you. I'll put you down as a witness." -> thanks
  node thanks rook "Go on, then. Be a better navigator than me. The bar's low and I'm under it. And boy: don't let them write you down as lost."
  node bye rook "A hurry. I remember those. Went everywhere in one, once."
